{
 "about": "A Cobra-bay launch (M7-T08, D76), after the maintainer's show GIFs: Starfuries are stored on the rack at 90 degrees to the launch, the clamp turns them nose-out while their door's toothed leaves slide apart, and they are ejected nose first, quickly (0.75 s from the rack past the door, 61 m/s at the release), a wave's doors firing in turn along the arm 0.25 to 0.5 s apart (a seeded draw per launch). Poses are in the door's frame (x across the arm, y out of the drum, z aft): forward is the nose, up the top. The camera comes in phases, each a pool of shot variants; every launch draws one variant a phase from a seeded shuffle bag (LaunchCut), and an optional phase is left out with its 'optional' chance. A phase plays once the player's fighter has been 'at_s' seconds in its step (door, rotate, hold, drop, release). Shots use the actors 'bay' (the launching door, same frame) and 'fighter' (the player's ship: -z its nose, +y its top). A key's 'up' keeps the picture upright against the arm (inside the hall toward the drum's axis, outside away from it); a variant's 'fill' is a light lit through the LightPicker for the shot's length only. 'gif' names the show frame a variant came from (references/, gitignored), when one did. Each variant's 'move' says the camera's move in one line (M8-T30, for the review sheets). No shot lasts 3 s or more unless flagged 'feature' (an interesting one, up to 5 s; maintainer, 2026-11-19): between phases the director cuts to other shots of the pool, none twice in one launch while unplayed ones remain.",
